{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Before you would fear.</b> You do not yet fear. And so every טֶרֶם in Scripture is 'not yet' — it is not a term of 'before.' ״טֶרֶם יִשְׁכְּבוּ״ (Genesis 19) — before they lay down [not yet]; ״טֶרֶם יִצְמָח״ (ibid. 2) — before it sprouted [not yet]. This too is so: 'I know that you are not yet God-fearers,' and once relief comes you will persist in your corruption."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:17.146369561Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}